{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Implemented schema migration in `in/schema_migration/client.py`.\n\nChanges:\n- Supports legacy v1, v1.1, v1.2, and already-v2 payloads.\n- Maps customer, order, line-item, shipping, and postal fields per migration notes.\n- Converts numeric strings to integers.\n- Defaults blank/null shipping methods to `\"standard\"`.\n- Preserves legacy unknown fields under `metadata.unknownFields`.\n- Drops configured PII keys from preserved legacy metadata.\n- Keeps v2 metadata and line items intact while normalizing nullable shipping methods.\n- Added `convert_many(payloads)` with aggregated errors containing `index`, `path`, and `error`.\n- Writes `conversion_audit.json` on every batch conversion.\n- Added `python -m client input.jsonl output.json` CLI support.\n\nVerification:\n- Python compilation succeeded.\n- Existing test functions executed successfully directly: `tests ok`.\n- Sample JSONL conversion succeeded: 4 converted, 0 errors.\n- CLI smoke check succeeded.\n- Generated audit:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"converted_count\": 4,\n  \"error_count\": 0,\n  \"warning_count\": 0,\n  \"pii_dropped_count\": 5,\n  \"unknown_fields_count\": 5\n}\n```\n\n`pytest` itself was unavailable in the environment (`No module named pytest`), so the test functions and equivalent conversion scenarios were executed directly."}}
